had his own Blood Bound female minion, Evelyn, exactly like the Prince. The Anarchs are not the Rebel Alliance and whenever they do take over a territory like Los Angeles or Berlin, it's a crapshot whether that territory will become better or worse for their influence. Being an Anarch means you're against the city's Elders and Prince, nothing more or less.<br /> <br /> <b>2:] Anarchs think they're the good guys</b><br /> <br /> Contradicting number 1# is the fact that many anarchs believe themselves to be the good guys or, at least, the lesser evil. Everything is relative in Cainite society and the fury over past injustices is a major reason why the Movement has not died in six hundred years. There are many idealistic voices among the Anarchs like Maldavis, Anita Wainwright, Jeremy MacNeil, Nines, and Salvador Garcia. Don't get me wrong, they're still ****ing vampires but they have legitimate greviances motivating them as well as a passionate belief things can get better. It's the presence of these individuals that prevents the entire Anarch experiment from being written off as just another bunch of Kindred warring for freedom.</div> </div> </div> </div>To a certain extent, yes. I still have trouble believing that high Humanity Anarchs are okay with certain super sketchy choices- I'm currently running<i> The Sacrifice </i>from <i>CBN V5 </i>and.. I don't know, something just feels off about three Humanity 8 vampires and a Humanity 7 vampire would be willing to use an absolute <i>monster</i> like Malenkov as a tool. MacTavish is no saint, but even he's better than Malenkov. Maybe they have the idea to use him, and then wash their hands of him when my players explain how bad he is. Depending on how well they RP it, Maldavis might even say that she's totally on board handing Malenkov over to Jackson.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T18:11:30-07:00","id":1384536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384526-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-anarchs?p=1384531#post1384531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely agree with a lot of this and another two things that I also want to note and admittedly CTPhipps has already touched on the former, but just something that I want to throw out as well for people looking into the Anarch Movement for the first time or just seeking to expand their understanding...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I had a few extra bits myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022The Anarch Movement is a broad spectrum of ideology and practice. While the name is naturally a reference to anarchism and much of the Movement's most well known aspects are drawn from leftist political theory and gang culture, the 'Anarch' moniker is something of a misnomer. Some Anarchs are indeed Anarchists or have Anarchist leanings or sympathies, but they are only one faction of many, under the vestigial title of 'Anarch'. Anarchs are across the spectrum of right-left, authoritarian-anarchist, secular-spiritual; etc. The Anarch Movement honestly can encompass any kindred ideology that is not the Camarilla or Sabbat and rejects the traditional despotism of the elders. Anarchs can and are everything from Anarcho-Communists, Gangland neo-feudalists, fascist brownshirts, authoritarian leftists, athenian democrats, tammany hall grifters, theocratic communes, and whatever else you can imagine. The Movement is leviathan. </div> </div> </div>I think that's a chief appeal for the Anarchs and me because you can use them to justify just about any new group coming into the city. The player characters can be Anarchs that are pro-democracy, pro-civil rights, and high humanity protectors of humans. Then can come in a wild murderous band of Brujah straight out of the Lost Boys or even a bunch of white supremacists. Since Anarchs freely Embrace, any group can potentially expand their own gang's size pretty heavily. You might also run into a city that's run like a military dictatorship with all Anarchs in the city being forced to swear allegiance to the General.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022The second point I wish to highlight is the youth of the Movement. The Anarch Movement, while as a culture is arguably half a millennium old, the heart blood of the Movement are young and recently embraced kindred. These are kindred who were born and raised in the era of democratic republics, parliaments, and freedom of speech and press. These are kindred who were scions of the Information Age and digital revolution. Individually they are far weaker and less influential then any elder but they also radically outnumber that elder and are most certainly better able to maneuver within the modern nights. Similarly these kindred are less likely to harbor the centuries old prejudices of their elders, making the Movement all the more appealing to those who the Ivory Tower never meant to represent. The V20 books 'Anarchs Unbound' is an excellent resource for this and a survey of the modern Anarch Movement with the understanding that by its nature, the Movement dominates and runs circles around the other sects where technology is concerned.<br /> <br /> I like all the sects but I've also always had a spot close to my heart for the Anarch Movement and I appreciate them finally receiving the credit and recognition they deserve after so many years of being forced to play second fiddle to the Camarilla and Sabbat alike. </div> </div> </div>Definitely, I agree. I tend to think there's been a Baby Boom among Kindred in the 20th century. Prior to the 20th century, things kept the Kindred's numbers in check but now the free embracing of so many have resulted in generations rising and people being spread throughout. I actually attribute it in-universe to the publishing of Dracula. Prior to Bram Stoker's work, no one knew what a vampire was but now everyone can survive on their own as they have a basic understanding of &quot;the rules&quot; even if the sunlight thing was more movies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384526-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-anarchs?p=1384534#post1384534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To a certain extent, yes. I still have trouble believing that high Humanity Anarchs are okay with certain super sketchy choices- I'm currently running<i> The Sacrifice </i>from <i>CBN V5 </i>and.. I don't know, something just feels off about three Humanity 8 vampires and a Humanity 7 vampire would be willing to use an absolute <i>monster</i> like Malenkov as a tool. MacTavish is no saint, but even he's better than Malenkov. Maybe they have the idea to use him, and then wash their hands of him when my players explain how bad he is. Depending on how well they RP it, Maldavis might even say that she's totally on board handing Malenkov over to Jackson.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually felt THE SACRIFICE erred a little too much on &quot;Sierra=Good&quot;, &quot;Malenkov=Bad&quot; as I totally believe that Sierra actually knew going in that Kevin Jackson was going to need a sacrifice and brought her brother to kill. It sort of fits with the Cain and Abel vision of the Sabbat and really why so many Lasombra probably went along with it. Malenkov is a monster but when I ran the Sacrifice, I emphasized the fact he's not the sort of man who would EVER betray one of his fellow Lasombra, let alone his blood-sister this way. Indeed, his anger is because he's being forced to choose between loyalty to his sect and loyalty to his sire as well as Clan.<br /> <br /> So Malenkov is someone who might not actually be a complete fuck up among the Anarchs. He's a vicious psychopath and killer but he was &quot;acting out&quot; and is used to taking orders. Point him at enough Camarilla targets and interrogate him of all the secrets you can get and he'll do it. However, he could easily just diablerize an Anarch leader for weakness and start making the locals into proto-Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Really, while I think they were emphasizing Helena has been a toxic influence on Maldavis (and she's not happy that Anita and Gengis are making her irrelevant), I think a better choice to contact the PCs about keeping Malenkov alive would have been Anita herself. I feel she's more likely to believe he can be redeemed or &quot;re-adjusted.&quot; Even then, it would probably be a mistake. I would also put Malenkov on the Path of Honorable Accord. Maybe only at a 3 because he's lost some points due to having to betray his sect.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, Maldavis is speaking for Helena who intends to Dominate, Presence, and Bloodbond Malenkov into being her new bodyguard. Sect is meaningless to the Methuselah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-28-2020, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T18:25:43-07:00","id":1384539,"title":"","content":"My characters have &quot;Punish the wicked&quot; as a Chronicle Tenet. After the fight with Malenkov in the brothel, I can't see them letting him go. Anita as the main driver to save Malenkov is something that didn't occur to me. The PCs have yet to meet the Lasombra yet- they only managed to diffuse the trouble-makers in our first session- so I'm definitely looking forward to seeing that go down. Malenkov as &quot;angry confused soldier facing impending obsolescence&quot; is an angle I might try playing up. I don't think Talley sent him to die- Sierra is the one who sets the terms for the deal. Sierra is only using Malenkov as her sacrifice because she hates him. I'm planning on that selfish desire to eliminate her blood-brother to come back to bite her in the ass when she finds out Talley is marked for death by the Amici Noctis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T19:05:45-07:00","id":1384542,"title":"","content":"It's kind of hard for the Sabbat to be popular when there aren't any rules for running them yet even though V5 has been out for over a year, and Kuei-jin don't exist at all. So yeah if you want to play a vampire that isn't in the Camarilla your only options are Anarch and Autarkis and the latter isn't really a faction but the lack of a faction. So while some of the popularity is due to good portrayals the other is because the system currently supports them and not others. To be clear I am not saying that V5 is bad, merely pointing out that it has removed an option and when you can't play something it makes it hard to be popular.<br /> <br /> Something else that should be mentioned in regards to the whole enemy of my enemy is my enemy. There's another reason for the Anarchs to gravitate to the Camarilla when push comes to shove, the Camarilla let them exist. Following the Anarch Revolt the Treaty of Thorns brought the Anarchs back into the Camarilla and gave them some freedom to act. Of course as with all things related to vampires, the extent to this being recognized varied from Prince to Prince region to region. There was a reason the Prince didn't just send a bunch of ghouls to deal with the Anarchs during the daytime. Essentially they had to wait until the Anarchs broke the rules (hence why the Camarilla could move against the Free States since the Anarchs attacked and seized Camarilla domains).<br /> <br /> However I wonder how the hell Theo Bell is seen as a mediator between the Camarilla and Anarchs. He killed two of the Camarilla's leading figures during the debacle that was the Convention of Prague. He shouldn't be a liaison, he should be one of the top vampires on the Red List. &quot;As a mediator his judgement cant be faulted&quot;? Unless he decides to blow your head off in a peace conference, fairly certain there could be some fault to be found there. It was one of those things that struck me as completely out of place as I read the V5 rulebook. Considering it was the Brujah elders that pushed for leniency for the Anarchs, after they left I could have easily seen the Camarilla deciding to take a turn against the Brujah. They'd already gotten a pass once, and their curse made them prone to frenzy and thus a masquerade threat. Theo Bell's actions and the subsequent exodus of the Brujah should have left them as some of the most hated outsiders and Bell as one of the worst traitors of the sect. Unlike the Gangrel they didn't just leave, they killed on their way out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T19:45:03-07:00","id":1384545,"title":"","content":"What do you guys think of the idea of William Randolph Hearst being an ally/patron of the early Anarch movement and maybe even helping out with the creation of the L.A. Free State?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T19:59:22-07:00","id":1384547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cynic01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384526-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-anarchs?p=1384542#post1384542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's kind of hard for the Sabbat to be popular when there aren't any rules for running them yet even though V5 has been out for over a year, and Kuei-jin don't exist at all. So yeah if you want to play a vampire that isn't in the Camarilla your only options are Anarch and Autarkis and the latter isn't really a faction but the lack of a faction. So while some of the popularity is due to good portrayals the other is because the system currently supports them and not others. To be clear I am not saying that V5 is bad, merely pointing out that it has removed an option and when you can't play something it makes it hard to be popular.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm generally thinking overall. The Anarchs are one of the most popular sects of the game because there's the Anarchs, Kuei-Jin, Sabbat, Camarilla, Hecate, Ashirra, True Hand, Independents as a whole, Laibon, and so on. Even if they're ranked number 3# of the most popular, that's still pretty high up the list. I agree with you that the Sabbat should have been one of the supplements they released and I don't know why they are holding off releasing them so long. Even if you hate them as playable characters, which is a bit judgy of playstyles, they've been a staple antagonist since the beginning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Something else that should be mentioned in regards to the whole enemy of my enemy is my enemy. There's another reason for the Anarchs to gravitate to the Camarilla when push comes to shove, the Camarilla let them exist. Following the Anarch Revolt the Treaty of Thorns brought the Anarchs back into the Camarilla and gave them some freedom to act. Of course as with all things related to vampires, the extent to this being recognized varied from Prince to Prince region to region. There was a reason the Prince didn't just send a bunch of ghouls to deal with the Anarchs during the daytime. Essentially they had to wait until the Anarchs broke the rules (hence why the Camarilla could move against the Free States since the Anarchs attacked and seized Camarilla domains). </div> </div> </div>The problem with active war against the Anarchs is the fact that they're a rather tenancious enemy that I think the Camarilla might not be able to crush long term. The Camarilla HAS crushed the Anarchs repeatedly since the Convention of Thorns with the French Revolution being an example of the Elders losing ground, only to win in the end. Lodin also did crush the Anarchs, TWICE, with Modius and Maldavis but the threat never really left his city either. Part of this is just the nature of Kindred society. The only way to make a opening to ascend to you is kill the guy above you and the best way to do that is get everyone on the outs to support you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However I wonder how the hell Theo Bell is seen as a mediator between the Camarilla and Anarchs. He killed two of the Camarilla's leading figures during the debacle that was the Convention of Prague. He shouldn't be a liaison, he should be one of the top vampires on the Red List. &quot;As a mediator his judgement cant be faulted&quot;? Unless he decides to blow your head off in a peace conference, fairly certain there could be some fault to be found there. It was one of those things that struck me as completely out of place as I read the V5 rulebook. Considering it was the Brujah elders that pushed for leniency for the Anarchs, after they left I could have easily seen the Camarilla deciding to take a turn against the Brujah. They'd already gotten a pass once, and their curse made them prone to frenzy and thus a masquerade threat. Theo Bell's actions and the subsequent exodus of the Brujah should have left them as some of the most hated outsiders and Bell as one of the worst traitors of the sect. Unlike the Gangrel they didn't just leave, they killed on their way out. </div> </div> </div>I tend to agree that Theo Bell should probably be in hiding among the Anarchs rather than someone that should be a mediator after his stunt at Thorns. However, if I were to handle it, I would take a page out of YAKUZA the video game. I just finished Yakuza Zero and the plot of that game was the internal war between various factions over the actions of one of their members that exposed some bigger rifts in the organization.<br /> <br /> Theo Bell killing Hardestadt should have resulted in all of the <b>Hardliners</b> wanting him dead as well as trying to nominate him for the Red List. They're the guys who expelled the Brujah and removed the Prince of Berlin to install an Anti-Anarch one. They would normally be in ascendance and ready to pounce--but it has been 8 years. The Convention of Prague was in 2012 and it's now 2020.<br /> <br /> Those eight years haven't been kind to the hardliners.<br /> <br /> Berlin has been lost to the Camarilla, the Anarchs are now a 3 Clan Sect, and the Free States are now larger than ever. The Camarilla has recruited the Banu Haqim and maybe the Lasombra but its victories over the Sabbat have actually gotten them a newer enemy. The <b>Softliners</b>, who may have hated Hardestadt to begin with, may want to try to reconcile with the Anarchs or at least not annihilate them because the hardliners have utterly failed to get any traction with them.<br /> <br /> They may opposite putting Bell on the Red List, at least versus eliminating a more traditional way or playing the long game. After all, right now he's one of the few Anarch leaders that CAN be negotiated with right now since he's one of the only leaders and organizers they have with national attention. He's also not an ideologue to the Anarch cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-28-2020, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T20:01:32-07:00","id":1384548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384526-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-anarchs?p=1384545#post1384545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys think of the idea of William Randolph Hearst being an ally/patron of the early Anarch movement and maybe even helping out with the creation of the L.A. Free State?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting possibility and I could actually justify it right out of the bat. You have one of the richest men in America and most influential embraced by, say, someone who isn't a Ventrue or Toreador only to say that he's excluded from the proper clubs (which is nothing new to Hearst).<br /> <br /> I would say he'd immediately do his best to try to strike out at them even as he slowly rebuilds his fortune and influence behind the scenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T20:02:35-07:00","id":1384549,"title":"","content":"It is worth remembering that Anarch have as many posers as does the Camarilla, namely ones who talk smack but are just all talk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T20:03:43-07:00","id":1384550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384526-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-anarchs?p=1384549#post1384549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is worth remembering that Anarch have as many posers as does the Camarilla, namely ones who talk smack but are just all talk.</div> </div> </div> </div>To summarize Gengis, Gengis is a Anarch who couldn't stand to exist without the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> He needs something to rebel against to justify his existence.<br /> <br /> As such, he's happy to toady to Kevin Jackson in private if it means he can tell him to piss off in public.<br /> <br /> So the perfect Anarch poseur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T21:47:13-07:00","id":1384570,"title":"","content":"I have a problem with the embrace of too many historical figures on principle, but if Hearst absolutely must be a vampire, he's obviously a Ventrue. He was a monopolist, for crying out loud.<br /> <br /> Now: Orson Welles, the artist whose feature length satirization of Hearst still stands as one of the greatest films ever made? There's your Toreador Anarch, right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T22:54:16-07:00","id":1384576,"title":"","content":"I added this tidbit:<br /> <br /> <i>There are also plenty of cross-sect friendships [or at least alliances] among Anarchs and Camarilla vampires unlike both organizations' members with the Sabbat. Victor Temple has a &quot;friendship&quot; of sorts with Fiorenza for example, their Clan Ventrue ties trumping sect allegiance. Until recently, most Anarchs were considered part of the Camarilla even if it was only nominally so. More cynical vampires also point out that Barons and Princes are two variations on the same word. Just not within earshot of either. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-29-2020, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T03:17:32-07:00","id":1384607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384526-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-anarchs#post1384526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>10:] My enemy of my enemy is my enemy</b><br /> <br /> Anarchs hate the Camarilla more than anything other than their other enemies. This is because a comfortable familiar enemy is as good as a friend in Kindred society. Anarchs will usually side with the Camarilla against the Sabbat, work to preserve the Masquerade, and even fight against each other if they can justify the other Anarchs being &quot;traitors.&quot; This is actually applicable to the Camarilla as well since they have often preferred to bribe, co-opt, or undermine the Anarchs than actually destroy them. Just a reminder that the Anarchs are long on rhetoric but only big on action that benefits them personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>wrong,<br /> the Anarchs are just as ready to ally with the sabbat/KJ as they are to ally to the Cam,<br /> <br /> the difference is...the Cam allows them to keep calling themselves anarchs,<br /> the ones that ally with the sabbat, however, simply become Sabbat <br /> the ones that ally with the kuei-jin become...well, some weird name I guess<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T04:00:52-07:00","id":1384613,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> thank you! Appreciate the support. I love your idea. And I really like the character of Gengis. I know more than one person of both genders who is exactly like that.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11599\" data-vbnamecard=\"11599\">Reasor</a> I agree 100%. But it happens sometimes, especially when the Anarchs don\u2019t give af about the Camarilla\u2019s rule about not Embracing famous people. Plus Hearst wasn\u2019t like a celebrity or anything. He was paranoid about his privacy, lived in a literal castle in the desert and preferred to manipulate things from behind the scenes (one reason he got so pissed at Citizen Kane).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T07:01:33-07:00","id":1384646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384526-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-anarchs?p=1384607#post1384607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> wrong,<br /> the Anarchs are just as ready to ally with the sabbat/KJ as they are to ally to the Cam,<br /> <br /> the difference is...the Cam allows them to keep calling themselves anarchs,<br /> the ones that ally with the sabbat, however, simply become Sabbat<br /> the ones that ally with the kuei-jin become...well, some weird name I guess</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I'm pretty sure that when you join the Sabbat you cease to be an Anarch.<br /> <br /> Hence, why it doesn't work that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T11:43:13-07:00","id":1385436,"title":"","content":"I feel the Theo Bell liason thing might work if you consider that it might be understood that he moved under supernatural compulsion.<br /> <br /> <br /> But on the money thing.<br /> The Text I can agree with; I imagine a lot of Anarchs hide their wealth. But I also imagine that, like modern gang leaders, many Anarchs show off and exaggerate their success in order to entice new prospects and present the anarch lifestyle as one for winners. But the header... You need like five different *'s to add here. While many anarchs aren't rich, most are comfortable. Most would be considered bourgiouse in that they &quot;own&quot; people who own private businesses. Apart from freshfaced fledglings and some people that have chosen to be poor, most anarchs have access to at least one dot of resources, which an undead creature can live easily off, without actually putting effort in. More live at a comfortable 2 or 3 resources. If you're not buying food and you're sharing a home, one dot of resources is enough for good clothes, transport, a gun in the US, especially when you consider a vampire's ability to save up over the years. Anarchs aren't working poor struggling each day to make ends meet. They're selling a lie.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also: <br /> Anarchs grow up. <br /> The vampires who live a long time are mostly smart. While social justice might be very important for humans, sooner or later a vampire will realise they're actually kinda bad for their existence. Vampires need people to be marginalized and impoverished so that it's easier to feed from them and the risk of being caught is lower. It might be terrible to live in a place where if someone got raped and nobody reports it because they're convinced it would do more harm than good, but that's paradise for vampires. That's exactly what vampires need to have a stable place in the ecosystem. Sure, they may enter unlife earnestly championing a cause, but unless the problems outweigh the benefits, they're going to get cynical real soon. Anarchs, as people championing themselves as the good guys, of course keep up appearances, but what they're really thinking by the time they're about a hundred...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 05-03-2020, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T11:56:41-07:00","id":1385438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384526-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-anarchs?p=1385436#post1385436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel the Theo Bell liason thing might work if you consider that it might be understood that he moved under supernatural compulsion.<br /> <br /> <br /> But on the money thing.<br /> The Text I can agree with; I imagine a lot of Anarchs hide their wealth. But I also imagine that, like modern gang leaders, many Anarchs show off and exaggerate their success in order to entice new prospects and present the anarch lifestyle as one for winners. But the header... You need like five different *'s to add here. While many anarchs aren't rich, most are comfortable. Most would be considered bourgiouse in that they &quot;own&quot; people who own private businesses. Apart from freshfaced fledglings and some people that have chosen to be poor, most anarchs have access to at least one dot of resources, which an undead creature can live easily off, without actually putting effort in. More live at a comfortable 2 or 3 resources. If you're not buying food and you're sharing a home, one dot of resources is enough for good clothes, transport, a gun in the US, especially when you consider a vampire's ability to save up over the years. Anarchs aren't working poor struggling each day to make ends meet. They're selling a lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think our differences in how we view resources. Personally, I'm referring to 4 and 5 Resources. I think the Camarilla has a vastly larger percentage of the 1% than the Anarchs with the majority of Elders controlling entire industries and infrastructure of the cities that they live in. The sheer difference in the level of resources is tremendous with the Anarchs not able to affect national policy the way that the camarilla can.<br /> <br /> The fact that a Anarch has an apartment they don't pay rent on or need to worry about food (because they hunt it) is an entirely different <i>kind</i> of wealth, let alone scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T12:56:09-07:00","id":1385448,"title":"","content":"The &quot;1%&quot; is really the better part of 3 dots of resources if we just include, say, the US. 4 dots is 0.1, 5 dots is 0.01%. Each dot is an exponent of the former, If we use this model of growth... We still don't match Jeff Bezos with dots of resource, dude is above 10. <br /> <br /> If we go worldwide, 2 dots of resources is &quot;the 1%&quot; but.. anyhow, point being even if we just accounted for the &quot;developed&quot; world, most anarchs are comfortably top 20%, most are 1%, I'll grant that they'll have fewer 0.01%ers, but that's largely because anarchs are younger, not because they're inherently poorer. Now, sure &quot;The 1%&quot; typically means multimillionaires in parlance if you're not talking about bikers, but statistically, Anarchs would be loaded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T12:58:38-07:00","id":1385449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384526-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-anarchs?p=1385448#post1385448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;1%&quot; is really the better part of 3 dots of resources if we just include, say, the US. 4 dots is 0.1, 5 dots is 0.01%. Each dot is an exponent of the former, If we use this model of growth... We still don't match Jeff Bezos with dots of resource, dude is above 10.<br /> <br /> If we go worldwide, 2 dots of resources is &quot;the 1%&quot; but.. anyhow, point being even if we just accounted for the &quot;developed&quot; world, most anarchs are comfortably top 20%, most are 1%, I'll grant that they'll have fewer 0.01%ers, but that's largely because anarchs are younger, not because they're inherently poorer. Now, sure &quot;The 1%&quot; typically means multimillionaires in parlance if you're not talking about bikers, but statistically, Anarchs would be loaded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm not referring to that. I mean Rich-Rich as money as a form of power. Yes, most Anarchs are not homeless.<br /> <br /> However, few Anarchs are above Resources 3 and many have less.<br /> <br /> Versus the Camarilla where MOST have higher.<br /> <br /> It may be different at your table, but that's just how I view it. It's important to emphasize the Anarchs being working class vs. super-rich. The class war element is important in my games.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T13:20:12-07:00","id":1385452,"title":"","content":"But they're not working class. They don't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T14:05:53-07:00","id":1385455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384526-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-anarchs?p=1385452#post1385452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they're not working class. They don't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote Baba O'Riley:<br /> <br /> <i>Out here in the fields<br /> <b>I fight for my meals</b><br /> I get my back into my living.</i><br /> <i>I don't need to fight</i><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Every Anarch has to work for their food because they don't have the big herds. One of the biggest reasons the Anarchs are rebelling is the fact they don't have enough Domain, feeding grounds, Herd, or influence to cover up their problems. They don't have the resources because they're the poorer cousins of the Camarilla and it restricts them. The Anarchs fight to free up some of that for themselves.<br /> <br /> At least in part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-03-2020, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T03:51:23-07:00","id":1385571,"title":"","content":"But they still don't work for money. We're discussing money. Are you going to call Mark Zuckerberg working class because he has to work to appear human? Do rich and powerful Camarilla vampires become working class when they go to hunt? Ridiculous!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T05:40:18-07:00","id":1385593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1384526-essay-top-ten-tips-to-running-anarchs?p=1385571#post1385571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they still don't work for money. We're discussing money. Are you going to call Mark Zuckerberg working class because he has to work to appear human? Do rich and powerful Camarilla vampires become working class when they go to hunt? Ridiculous!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Anarchs don't have much in the way of money, territory, or influence. Some do but they're much poorer on the average than the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> I don't trhink we're going to agree on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T13:54:09-07:00","id":1385928,"title":"","content":"My input for using Anarchs in games:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Michael Jackson Syndrome</u></b> Vampires without a sect can go decades without meeting a peer. This situation, especially given social disciplines and the blood bond, tends to breed wacky behavior. Think of the top-tier celebrities and billionaires who are completely insulated from consequences by their privilege. When you're surrounded by toadies, every idea you have seems awesome. Expect Anarchs and Autarkis to lead bizarre unlives, unfettered by any sense of morality, dignity, or even self-preservation.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Culture Lag</u></b> Anarchs make lots of noise about keeping up with the modern world, but an Anarch embraced in 1950 is still carrying the viewpoints, preferences, and prejudices of their breathing days. This can lead to nostalgia for passe ideals, from Soviet collectivism and Eugenics, to Apartheid apologetics and One-Nation Toryism. Beyond big ideological fights, expect friction between vampires with different embrace dates over everything from gender-neutral pronouns, to the Baron insisting on watching the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t8tdmaEhMHE\" target=\"_blank\">Lawence Welk</a> show every Saturday night.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Most Powerful Alliance is Always Apathy and Convenience</u></b> Most people, and most vampires, don't organize their lives around the political label they wear. Don't expect npcs to sacrifice their lives, fortunes, or even their convenience to the Cause, unless their is a significant chance it will improve their lives. If any sect makes a rule that you have to be poor to be a member, expect them to hemorrhage members.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Meanwhile, Back In The Boring Details</u></b> Just because the Anarchs win, and take over a city, it <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/DystopiaIsHard\" target=\"_blank\">doesn't mean they have succeeded</a>. The Camarilla has spent centuries running vampire governments with a mixed record. They have a formula that mostly works. Given there are no experts in public-administration doing best-practices surveys, it's hard to know what can be changed and what can't without disaster. Expect newly &quot;liberated&quot; domains to have all sorts of unexpected problems caused by their lack of a bureaucratic mindset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-05T16:40:45-07:00","id":1385973,"title":"","content":"Something that the prior post reminded me of is another part of the Anarch Movement that I'm thinking of is the co-morbidity between Anarch-Autarkis-Outcast communities with Outcasts basically referring to Caitiff and Thin-Bloods who largely can't exist in sect society without serious personal compromises and sacrifices.<br /> <br /> While different Anarchs will have different opinions and different levels of tolerance and acceptance, compared to the Camarilla and Sabbat, the Anarch Movement is in many respects the greatest opportunity for Autarkis and Outcasts to enter mainstream vampiric society as well as the protection of a sect.<br /> <br /> The Autarkis certainly exist on a spectrum but they represent a variety of political and social outcasts from mainstream vampiric society. From outlaws to loners to rejects, Autarkis have left typical vampiric society and for those interested in returning the Movement provides the most opportunity.<br /> <br /> The Outcasts such as Caitiff &amp; Thin-Bloods are unable to participate in most vampiric society due to their nature. The Anarch Movement however provides them both communal security and access to vampiric politics on some mainstream level as the Movement is willing to allow and support Caitiff and Thin-Bloods within their ranks. Considering the position of the scourge, this creates a rather fun sense of irony to me in that the Camarilla has indirectly become the largest recruiting mechanism the Anarch Movement has.<br /> <br /> I think that Autarkis and Outcasts are often over looked and I hope that this helps people consider how they might use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-06T04:20:45-07:00","id":1386038,"title":"","content":"It's a libertarian VS Conservative conflic<br /> <br /> another way to see it, It's the American war of independence. <br /> <br /> From the Cam perspective: After the Camarilla had waged an expensive war against the Sabbat/Inquisition, A bunch of rich folk didn't want to pay taxes, so they cooked up a lot of noble sounding ideas, applied some fantastic slogans, and conned some neonates into fighting for them against the Camarilla <br /> <br /> From the Anarch perspective: FREEEEEEEDOOOOOM!!!! USA! USA! USA! <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Oh wait the common people are worse off now? </i></span><br /> <br /> <br /> (Maybe once the vampires have their &quot;world war 2&quot; the Anarchs can rise as a power, but not yet.) <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}